 If there is no old in text, pass does nothing. If max_rounds is unreachable, we might stop after max_rounds, then fixed_point=False.\n\nCheck example payload: text \"aaaa bb cc\", passes: halve-a (replace \"aa\" with \"a\"), drop-b (replace \"bb\" with \"b\"), drop-c (replace \" cc\" with \"\"). First round: halve-a: find \"aa\" at index 0? \"aaaa\": first occurrence of \"aa\" at index0, replace with \"a\" => \"aa bb cc\". Then drop-b: find \"bb\" at index 3? after space? \"aa bb cc\" -> find \"bb\" at index 3 (if zero-indexed: \"aa bb cc\": positions: 0:a,1:a,2:space,3:b,4:b,5:space,...) replace with \"b\" => \"aa b cc\". Then drop-c: find \" cc\" at index? \"aa b cc\": find \" cc\" (space+cc) at index 3? Actually after b is space then cc: \"aa b cc\": indices: 0:a,1:a,2:space,3:b,4:space,5:c,6:c. So \" cc\" starts at 4? Actually \" cc\" includes the leading space. So index 4? Let's compute: substring \" cc\" at index4 (space at 4, c at5, c at6). Replace with \"\" -> \"aa b\". So after first round, text = \"aa b\". Second round: halve-a: find \"aa\" at index0 -> replace with \"a\" -> \"a b\". drop-b: find \"bb\"? not present, skip. drop-c: find \" cc\"? not present, skip. So changed_in_round True. Third round: halve-a: find \"aa\"? not present (\"a b\" has no \"aa\"), skip all -> no change, fixed_point True. applications: list of passes applied in order: halve-a (round1), drop-b (round1), drop-c (round1), halve-a (round2). So [\"halve-a\", \"drop-b\", \"drop-c\", \"halve-a\"].\n\nBut wait: The task says \"Record only passes that change the artifact.\" That matches.\n\nAlright. Implementation: simple Python function. Must raise ValueError for invalid case? The instruction says \"Raise ValueError for an infeasible or structurally invalid case instead of silently repairing it.\" So we should validate inputs: text must be string, passes must be list of dicts with required keys, old/new strings, max_rounds positive int? Probably not required in spec but we can check. We'll keep it simple: ensure all fields exist and types. If not, raise ValueError.\n\nThe code must be in Python source as JSON string. Write the solve function.\n\nAlso note: The fixture payload includes _case_nonce which is irrelevant. We ignore that.\n\nWrite the code, then embed in JSON.\n\nMake sure to escape correctly.\n\nOutput: {\"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    # validation ...\\n    ...\\n    return result\"}\n\nWe'll write compact but readable.\n\nPotential pitfall: The pass schedule must use \"first eligible rewrite per sweep\" meaning we do at most one replacement per pass per sweep. That's what we did: find first occurrence, replace, continue. That's correct.\n\nAnother nuance: The passes are registered in order; we must preserve that order. The list case['passes'] already gives order.\n\nNow produce final answer."},"logprobs":null,"finish_reason":"stop"}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":1310,"completion_tokens":1680,"total_tokens":2990,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":1280},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":1208},"prompt_cache_hit_tokens":1280,"prompt_cache_miss_tokens":30},"system_fingerprint":"fp_8b330d02d0_prod0820_fp8_kvcache_20260402"}